    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61231" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλῆ</span></b> , ἡ, 
			contr.
		 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλέα</span>, which occurs in
			<i><span class="en">
			Anaxipp.
			1.38
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			LXX
			<u>1 Ki.</u>
			9.24
		</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλία</span></b>  (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλίαν</span>) is a dialectal form: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶλον</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thighbone with the flesh on it, ham</i>, esp. of a
			swine, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				224
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				50.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				17
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Amips.
				7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίφου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					6.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοὸς κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Lex.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; the portion of the priestess at a sacrifice, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1361.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1015.10
			</span></i> (Halic.), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>membrum virile</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				989
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1019
			</span></i>.</div>
